  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Two gunmen open fire during a Hanukkah celebration at Bondi Beach in Sydney, Australia, killing 15 people and leaving 42 others injured. One perpetrator is killed, while the other is arrested. Two bombs are found at the scene and detonated by police. ((News.au)) ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Thailand confirms that a rocket launched from Cambodia killed a Thai villager, the first civilian death in Thailand as a result of the ongoing conflict. ((AP))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Hamas Lieutenant Colonel Ahmed Zamzam is shot and killed by a gunman inside the Maghazi refugee camp in the Deir al-Balah Governorate, Gaza Strip. The perpetrator is arrested. ((Palestine Chronicle)) ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Three people are killed in three separated Israeli airstrikes against vehicles in southern Lebanon. ((L'Orient Today))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Four security force members are killed and another is injured in a mass shooting when gunmen open fire on a patrol in Idlib, Syria. ((TRT World))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "A school bus in Remedios, Colombia, falls off a cliff, killing 17 people and injuring 20 others. The victims, all students from the same school, were returning home after a school-sponsored excursion. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "A person of interest is taken into custody for yesterday's mass shooting that killed two people and injured nine others at Brown University in Providence, Rhode Island, United States. The person is later released from custody the same day, with authorities announcing that they are still searching for a suspect. ((CNN)) ((The New York Times))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "Guatemalan president Bernardo Arévalo declares a state of emergency in two municipalities in western Guatemala a day after gunmen attacked a military post and a police station, cut off roads, and hijacked buses, killing at least five people. ((CityNews Halifax))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "Chileans vote for their president in a runoff between Jeannette Jara and José Antonio Kast. ((AP))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "Kast, the Republican Party candidate, is projected as the president-elect of Chile. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "Czech president Petr Pavel appoints prime minister Andrej Babiš's cabinet following ANO's victory in the recent election. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "At least 37 people are killed and 14 more injured during flash floods in Safi, Morocco. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "A school bus carrying students returning from a field trip falls off a cliff in Remedios, Colombia, killing 17 people and injuring 20 others. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "A school bus carrying students returning from a field trip falls off a cliff in Remedios, Antioquia, Colombia, killing 17 people and injuring 20 others. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "Kast is elected president of Chile. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "American filmmaker and actor Rob Reiner and his wife Michele Singer Reiner are stabbed to death at their home in Los Angeles, California, United States. Their son, Nick, is latter charged with the alleged murders. ((NBC News)), ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "American filmmaker and actor Rob Reiner and his wife Michele Singer Reiner are stabbed to death at their home in Los Angeles, California, United States. Their son, Nick, is later charged with the alleged murders. ((NBC News)), ((BBC News))"
    }
